ransportation can know the position of the truck thanks to the GPS in the track\(\))/CreationDate(D:20170211150901+01'00')/F 28/M(D:20170212110901+01'00')/NM(f6b76e53-6311-4ab7-b376-ae45582b6756)/Name/Comment/P 66 0 R/Popup 1504 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:15.23.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-\weight:normal;font-style:normal">Not all the actors in the value chain have access to them \(some are manifest, some others not\). e.g. parts can be singularly known in the production process or internal logistic chain, but, when palletized and given to t\he external logistic chain, the only identifiable object \(by the logistic carrier\) is the pallet not the parts while the company continues to know each component within the pallet, but, in standard transport only their global position is updated \(not i\n continuous way\).&#13;&#13;In the present case of logistics the company that manages the transportation can know the position of the truck thanks to the GPS in the track\(\)</span></p></body>)/Rect[451.799 242.937 469.799 260.937]/Subj(Nota)/Subtype/Text/T(Gualtiero Fantoni)/Type/Annot>>endobj1504 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 1503 0 R/Rect[411.967 173.601 592.185 315.419]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj1505 0 obj<</BBox[67.3857 307.626 562.284 333.89]/Filter[/FlateDecode]/FormType 1/Length 147/Matrix[1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -67.3857 -307.626]/Resources<</ProcSet[/PDF]>>/Subtype/Form/Type/XObject>>stream
